From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LS1046A integration <maintainers@vyos.net>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] http-api: add Model Context Protocol (MCP) server (default off)

Mounts an MCP Streamable-HTTP endpoint at /mcp/ inside the existing
vyos-http-api-server (FastAPI), proxied through nginx. Exposes operational
commands, config read/modify, image management, and schema introspection as
MCP tools, resources and prompts for AI-agent integration.

Config: `set service https api mcp mode <read-only|read-write>` and
`set service https api mcp introspection`. The node is absent by default,
so the endpoint ships DORMANT (off) until explicitly configured.

Authorization is enforced, not just advertised:
  - read-only sessions expose only execute_operational_command; hidden write
    tools are not callable and mutating op-mode verbs are rejected.
  - schema introspection is refused by direct URI when disabled.
Prompts are mode-aware and schema-driven. The capabilities overview reflects
the real read-only/introspection state. Home-oriented read-only prompts ship
by default: troubleshoot_internet_connectivity (WAN-down triage) and
analyze_security_posture (an educational, plain-language security review for
home users — WAN firewalling, IPv4/IPv6 parity, exposed management services,
and zone segmentation). VPN provisioning declares validated MCP arguments and
is exposed only for read-write sessions with introspection. Custom prompts
cannot shadow built-in safety/workflow prompts.

The mcp SDK and its Python deps are provided by the vyos-http-api-tools
virtualenv rebuilt with mcp==1.8.1 (see bin/ci-build-http-api-tools.sh), not a
system python3-mcp package; the fork's debian/control dependency is omitted.

Origin: mihakralj/vyos-1x branch T9030-mcp, with LS1046A hardening.

patch-series-cleanup (2026-09-11): split from the original all-in-one
patch. The 9 new src/services/api/mcp/*.py files carry no upstream
original to diff against ("new file mode" hunks ARE the file content) and
moved to data/vyos-1x-files/src/services/api/mcp/ as plain tracked source,
copied into place by ci-setup-vyos1x.sh's pre_build_hook before this patch
(and the rest of the series) applies. This patch now carries only the 4
hunks that genuinely modify pre-existing upstream files: wiring the /mcp/
route into nginx + the CLI schema + SessionState + the FastAPI app.
---
diff --git a/data/templates/https/nginx.default.j2 b/data/templates/https/nginx.default.j2
index 0f1a79ad7..7044867198 100644
--- a/data/templates/https/nginx.default.j2
+++ b/data/templates/https/nginx.default.j2
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@
     ssl_verify_depth 2;
 {% endif %}
     # proxy settings for HTTP API, if enabled; 503, if not
-    location ~ ^/(retrieve|configure|config-file|image|import-pki|container-image|generate|show|reboot|reset|poweroff|ping|traceroute|info|docs|openapi.json|redoc|graphql|renew|token) {
+    location ~ ^/(mcp|retrieve|configure|config-file|image|import-pki|container-image|generate|show|reboot|reset|poweroff|ping|traceroute|info|docs|openapi.json|redoc|graphql|renew|token) {
 {% if api is vyos_defined %}
         proxy_pass http://unix:/run/api.sock;
         proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
diff --git a/interface-definitions/service_https.xml.in b/interface-definitions/service_https.xml.in
index 3881c4b49..7209c541f 100644
--- a/interface-definitions/service_https.xml.in
+++ b/interface-definitions/service_https.xml.in
@@ -198,6 +198,39 @@
                   </node>
                 </children>
               </node>
+              <node name="mcp">
+                <properties>
+                  <help>Model Context Protocol (MCP) endpoint for AI agent integration</help>
+                </properties>
+                <children>
+                  <leafNode name="mode">
+                    <properties>
+                      <help>MCP tool access level</help>
+                      <completionHelp>
+                        <list>read-only read-write</list>
+                      </completionHelp>
+                      <valueHelp>
+                        <format>read-only</format>
+                        <description>Read configuration and run operational commands only</description>
+                      </valueHelp>
+                      <valueHelp>
+                        <format>read-write</format>
+                        <description>Additionally allow configuration changes and system management</description>
+                      </valueHelp>
+                      <constraint>
+                        <regex>(read-only|read-write)</regex>
+                      </constraint>
+                    </properties>
+                    <defaultValue>read-only</defaultValue>
+                  </leafNode>
+                  <leafNode name="introspection">
+                    <properties>
+                      <help>Expose schema introspection resources to AI agents</help>
+                      <valueless/>
+                    </properties>
+                  </leafNode>
+                </children>
+              </node>
             </children>
           </node>
           #include <include/allow-client.xml.i>
diff --git a/src/services/api/session.py b/src/services/api/session.py
index c1eb534d8..cf65edffc 100644
--- a/src/services/api/session.py
+++ b/src/services/api/session.py
@@ -45,3 +45,6 @@
         self.oidc_issuer = None
         self.oidc_jwks_uri = None
         self.oidc_audience = None
+        self.mcp = False
+        self.mcp_mode = 'read-only'
+        self.mcp_introspection = False
diff --git a/src/services/vyos-http-api-server b/src/services/vyos-http-api-server
index 6a420f499..aac536e46 100644
--- a/src/services/vyos-http-api-server
+++ b/src/services/vyos-http-api-server
@@ -231,6 +231,15 @@
     else:
         session.graphql = False

+    # parse the mcp block from api_config_state into SessionState
+    mcp_config = server_config.get('mcp', {})
+    if 'mcp' in server_config:
+        session.mcp = True
+        session.mcp_mode = mcp_config.get('mode', 'read-only')
+        session.mcp_introspection = bool('introspection' in mcp_config)
+    else:
+        session.mcp = False
+
     # pass session state
     app.state = session

@@ -250,6 +259,14 @@
         from api.graphql.routers import graphql_clear
         graphql_clear(app)

+    # add MCP route
+    if session.mcp:
+        from api.mcp.routers import mcp_init
+        mcp_init(app)
+    else:
+        from api.mcp.routers import mcp_clear
+        mcp_clear(app)
+
     regenerate_docs(app)

     LOG.debug('Active routes are:')
